                            <comment id="15136571" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 8 Feb 2016 03:33:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user asfgit closed the pull request at:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/657&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/657&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15253545" author="parasitid@yahoo.fr" created="Fri, 22 Apr 2016 08:37:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;hello &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=doanduyhai&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;doanduyhai&quot;&gt;doanduyhai&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;i work @ippon-technologies. i encounter several problems with the spark+cassandra integration on zeppelin.&lt;br/&gt;
and among them, the &quot;guava 16.0.1 dependency&quot; described in this issue. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;i don&apos;t think your patch solves it. &lt;br/&gt;
i&apos;ve build zeppelin from sources on the 21st of april, and the &quot;16.0.1&quot; exception still pop ups randomly.&lt;br/&gt;
when i debug the spark workers, i notice that there are several fatjars uploaded which contain diffenrent guava versions ( 15 and 14 ). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;so my spark jobs embeds guava 16.0.1, 14 &amp;amp; 15..... and it then relies on the classloader....&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;there are several pom.xml in zeppelin that defines guava versions. Couldn&apos;t we align them all at least on v16.0.1 ?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;here&apos;s a patch i&apos;m gonna test which adds a new profile for spark1.6+cassandra&lt;br/&gt;
and updates spark/pom.xml guava version from 14 to 16 version&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://pastebin.com/8Q8LJime&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://pastebin.com/8Q8LJime&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15253623" author="doanduyhai" created="Fri, 22 Apr 2016 09:36:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=parasitid%40yahoo.fr&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;parasitid@yahoo.fr&quot;&gt;parasitid@yahoo.fr&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; How did you &lt;b&gt;build&lt;/b&gt; zeppelin ? Can you copy paste the &lt;em&gt;mvn&lt;/em&gt; command ?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; If you&apos;re using &lt;b&gt;Spark 1.6&lt;/b&gt; there is NO maven profile YET to embedded the spark-cassandra connector. I&apos;m waiting for a stable release of the connector to propose a PR into Zeppelin. Right now the connector version is still in milestone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; For your own usage, you can add an extra profile &lt;em&gt;cassandra-spark-1.6&lt;/em&gt; and force Guava version to &lt;b&gt;16.0.1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15253686" author="parasitid@yahoo.fr" created="Fri, 22 Apr 2016 10:11:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi DOAN,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;that&apos;s what i&apos;ve done, cf the patch in the pastebin.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;the mvn command is &lt;br/&gt;
mvn clean package -DskipTests -Pcassandra-spark-1.5&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;yet i have another pb which is not really related to this issue : it seems that i have to add the spark-cassanda-connector as a dependency in the interpreter.json file. or else i get exceptions claiming that the com.datastax package is not found.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yet when i unzip the fatjar zeppelin-spark-dependencies, the connector is present....&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15253704" author="parasitid@yahoo.fr" created="Fri, 22 Apr 2016 10:23:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;do you have a slack chan or a gmail hangout account to discuss this ?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On Fri, Apr 22, 2016 at 11:36 AM, DOAN DuyHai (JIRA) &amp;lt;jira@apache.org&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="15253710" author="doanduyhai" created="Fri, 22 Apr 2016 10:28:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;doanduyhai at gmail dot com&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15253712" author="parasitid@yahoo.fr" created="Fri, 22 Apr 2016 10:28:44 +0000"  >
&lt;p&gt;FYI: the spark-cassandra-connector 1.5 is compatible with spark 1.6 ( cf : &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/datastax/spark-cassandra-connector&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/datastax/spark-cassandra-connector&lt;/a&gt; )&lt;br/&gt;
1.5	1.5, 1.6	2.1.5*, 2.2, 3.0	3.0&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
